THE CORE WHY
Storage has no DB cascade, so a storage column absent from these two functions
leaks its objects silently on account or property deletion. Migration 063 made
rental_payments file-bearing; this closes that.

Ownership resolves through properties.user_id, never the uploader path prefix.
A statement can legitimately be uploaded by an active co-owner guest, in which
case the object sits under the GUEST's id while the rental_payments row belongs
to the OWNER's property. A prefix scan would let the guest's account deletion
wipe the owner's evidence.

No SELECT DISTINCT on this branch, unlike depreciation_reports: one statement
maps to one payment row, so a path cannot repeat. The migration comment records
that this must change if a statement is ever allowed to span several rows.

DEVIATION FROM PLAN
docs/account-deletion.md was scheduled for Phase 6. Moved here because that
file carries the maintenance rule requiring its own table to be updated
whenever a file-bearing column is added; leaving it stale across five phases
would undercut the rule it states.

